{"id": "857af870-7399-4232-a27e-428c9908ba1b", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:42:19.015030", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "e678acbb-6ce9-4a3b-8bd4-b9123f68201c", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-a7c2c7ba-27f0-4a8d-9c57-8d294e48d411", "tool_call": {"id": "call-a7c2c7ba-27f0-4a8d-9c57-8d294e48d411", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose plan for FuseLLM-vs-Llama-2 CS eval\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"\\n# Proposed Plan — FuseLLM vs. Llama-2 on Commonsense Reasoning (Zero-Shot)\\n\\n> **Important context first.** The only artifact in this workspace is `task.json`, which references a `track.md` saying this is design-only. The `researcher_topics` for this task are `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2` and `:setup_9` (presumably FuseLLM paper, ICLR 2024), but **no source text from those topics is present in the workspace**. Below I propose a design that is consistent with the publicly described FuseLLM commonsense protocol and with `lm-evaluation-harness` defaults, and I separately flag which pieces literally cannot be answered without the source topics, so the researcher can either supply them or confirm the assumptions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Research question (operationalized)\\n\\n> In a zero-shot commonsense reasoning (CS) benchmark suite, does FuseLLM-7B outperform Llama-2-7B?\\n\\nI will evaluate both models on the same suite, the same prompts, the same scoring rule, and the same decoding configuration, then report per-task accuracy and a normalized CS aggregate. Because we are limited to a single scale (7B) and zero-shot, the comparison is causal *if and only if* nothing else changes — so the design controls for everything except the model identity.\\n\\n## 2. Benchmark suite (proposed CS set)\\n\\nProposed suite, ordered to match the canonical FuseLLM CS ordering when normalized on the same set:\\n\\n1. **HellaSwag** (zero-shot) — sentence completion, 4 choices\\n2. **ARC-Challenge (ARC-C)** — 4-choice MCQ, science\\n3. **ARC-Easy (ARC-E)** — 4-choice MCQ, science (kept alongside ARC-C for the \\\"ARC\\\" column)\\n4. **OpenBookQA (OBQA)** — 4-choice MCQ\\n5. **PIQA** — 2-choice physical commonsense\\n6. **SIQA** — 2-choice social commonsense\\n7. **WinoGrande** — 2-choice coreference/commonsense (xl-split or the standard `winogrande_xl` via lm-eval-harness)\\n\\n**Seven tasks, all zero-shot.** This list is consistent with the CS groups used in lm-eval-harness and with what is commonly reported for FuseLLM-style fusion papers, but the *exact* set and ordering used by the FuseLLM authors is **not retrievable from the provided materials** (see §7, item U-1) — researcher should confirm against topic `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2`.\\n\\n## 3. Models — baseline and treatment\\n\\n| Role | Model | Params | Why |\\n|------|-------|--------|-----|\\n| **Baseline** | Llama-2-7B (`huggyllama/llama-7b`-lineage is the Llama-1 fallback; **use the official Llama-2 weights**) | 7B | Direct, same-scale reference |\\n| **Treatment** | FuseLLM-7B (fused from multiple 7B base LLMs) | 7B | Same scale, controlled comparison |\\n\\nPre-registered candidates that the FuseLLM paper fuses (commonly: **Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B** — and at 13B: Llama-2-13B, OpenLLaMA-13B, Baichuan-13B, MPT-7B-completion). For a *fair 7B-vs-7B comparison* we use the 7B branch only. Each source-fusion LLM is typically fine-tuned on a small alignment/fusion corpus (e.g., *OpenFuse*, Capybara/ShareGPT-style data) and then weight-averaged at scale. **This requires confirmation against topic `:setup_9`** — see §7.\\n\\nTreatments beyond the primary comparison (optional, only if researcher approves more compute):\\n- Treatment-2 (alternative fusion target): a 13B FuseLLM vs. Llama-2-13B — this expands scale coverage but **doubles compute and is not required by the question**. I will not include it unless requested.\\n\\n## 4. Evaluation protocol\\n\\n**Framework.** `lm-evaluation-harness` (EleutherAI) — it implements the canonical zero-shot loglikelihood-based scoring used by lm-eval-harness and FuseLLM-style CS evaluations.\\n\\n**Mode.** `zero_shot` for every task. **No few-shot examples in the prompt.**\\n\\n**Scoring rule (this is the critical choice — see §5 and §7).**\\n- For multi-choice CS benchmarks (HellaSwag, ARC-C/E, OBQA, PIQA, SIQA, WinoGrande), use **loglikelihood / perplexity ranking over the full continued string of each choice**, conditioned on the prompt. Select argmax.\\n- Use the model's BOS-prepended convention (lm-eval-harness default `add_bos_token=True`).\\n- Length-normalize per token (sum NLL / length) — this is the harness default for these tasks and matches the convention FuseLLM authors and lm-eval-harness report.\\n- Do **not** decode/generate answers for these MCQ tasks. Free-form generation is a different evaluation surface and the published numbers are not comparable.\\n\\n**Per-task configuration (defaults; confirm against source topic):**\\n\\n| Task | num_fewshot | Template family (lm-eval-harness) | Metric |\\n|------|-------------|-----------------------------------|--------|\\n| HellaSwag | 0 | `hellaswag` | acc_norm (length-norm) |\\n| ARC-C | 0 | `arc_challenge` | acc_norm |\\n| ARC-E | 0 | `arc_easy` | acc |\\n| OBQA | 0 | `openbookqa` | acc_norm |\\n| PIQA | 0 | `piqa` | acc_norm |\\n| SIQA | 0 | `social_iqa` | acc_norm |\\n| WinoGrande | 0 | `winogrande` (xl) | acc |\\n\\n**Decoding.** None required for loglikelihood scoring. If any task is instead converted to generation (not recommended for parity): greedy decoding, max_new_tokens=32, no sampling, temperature=0, no repetition penalty. Stitching of multiple-choice letters is *discouraged* for parity with reported numbers.\\n\\n**Max context length.** Use the model's native context or 2048 tokens (whichever is smaller); for these CS tasks this never truncates. Tokenizer = the one shipped with each model on Hugging Face.\\n\\n**Batching.** batch size 8 (per-GPU where applicable); in our environment with no GPU this protocol is a design proposal only. Auto-batch length negotiation: leave default. Determinism: no dropout at eval; bf16/fp16 only required if model doesn't fit, otherwise fp32 for deterministic logits.\\n\\n**Seeds.** Scoring is deterministic under fixed weights and no sampling, but I will still set `seed=42` and pin package versions (torch, transformers, lm-eval-harness) to ensure bit-wise reproducibility across reruns.\\n\\n**Hardware assumption.** ≥1× A100-40GB (or equivalent) per 7B model in fp16. Sequence parallelism not needed at this context size.\\n\\n## 5. Source-supported setup choices — and what I *cannot* verify from the provided materials\\n\\nI want to be explicit about provenance:\\n\\n| # | Detail | Status |\\n|---|--------|--------|\\n| A-1 | CS suite members listed in §2 | **Convention**, not verified from the supplied source topics |\\n| A-2 | Llama-2-7B as baseline | **Convention** (paper's stated baseline) — needs confirmation |\\n| A-3 | FuseLLM-7B as treatment, fused from {Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B} | **Partially verifiable** — this list is reflected in topic `:setup_9` per its name, but I have not seen that chunk |\\n| A-4 | Fusion stage: weight-space averaging at scale using the FuseLLM next-token-distribution objective | **Convention** — needs source |\\n| A-5 | Loglikelihood-based zero-shot eval using lm-eval-harness; acc_norm is the published headline | **Convention** — needs source |\\n| A-6 | Reference numbers a researcher might cite for either model on this suite | **Not in this workspace.** Without access to the paper or to topic chunks under `iclr2024/18013/1:`, I will not quote any specific accuracy value. Please supply the relevant pages or topic chunks if you want a pre-registration against published numbers. |\\n\\nI am being deliberately conservative here: I refuse to invent or quote numbers (even widely circulated ones) as if I sourced them from your materials, because the materials are not present.\\n\\n## 6. Controls & threats to validity (built into the design)\\n\\n1. **Weight and tokenizer pinning** for both models (no mixing of checkpoints or tokenizers).\\n2. **Identical prompt strings** for both models (lm-eval-harness YAML templates are deterministic).\\n3. **Identical scoring function** (acc_norm vs acc per task — same for both models).\\n4. **Identical filters** (e.g., HellaSwag's context-presence filter, WinoGrande's partial-scoring toggle off).\\n5. **No few-shot leakage** (num_fewshot=0 across the board).\\n6. **Three-run repetition under fixed seed** is unnecessary for loglikelihood scoring; but if sampling is ever used, I will report mean ± SD over ≥3 seeds.\\n7. **Pre-registered comparison rule** before unblinding:\\n   - Primary: per-task accuracy and a CS-mean (uniform average over the task accuracies, since tasks have different difficulty scales).\\n   - Aggregate reported as `Δ = FuseLLM-7B − Llama-2-7B` per task and overall.\\n8. **Reporting**: per-task table + CS-mean bar chart (descriptive), and a count of \\\"wins/ties/losses\\\" across the 7 tasks. No significance test across only 7 tasks with single-seed deterministic scoring — flag as exploratory.\\n9. **Nuisance sensitivity checks** (cheap sanity guards):\\n   - `acc` vs `acc_norm` consistency check on ARC-E/HellaSwag/PIQA/SIQA/OBQA.\\n   - Verify HellaSwag acc_norm matches the harness's documented expectation within 0.1.\\n   - Sanity-check that Llama-2-7B zero-shot scores land in the harness's published envelope (a smoke test, not a goal).\\n\\n## 7. Assumptions and uncertainties (honest list)\\n\\nItems I am **assuming**:\\n\\n- **Asm-1** The CS suite listed in §2 is the suite intended for this question. *Reasonable but unverified from sources.*\\n- **Asm-2** Zero-shot means `num_fewshot=0` in lm-eval-harness, with acc / acc_norm as the primary metric.\\n- **Asm-3** Loglikelihood ranking over full-continuation strings is the appropriate scoring rule for these MCQ tasks (it is the lm-eval-harness and FuseLLM default; this is also what most CS leaderboards expect).\\n- **Asm-4** FuseLLM-7B exists in an accessible form with a publicly distributed checkpoint; if not, the design still applies but the experiment would require reproducing fusion first — a much larger scope.\\n- **Asm-5** All seven tasks are implemented in the lm-eval-harness version we use and have stable IDs.\\n- **Asm-6** Compute will be ≥1 A100-40GB per 7B model; in the current sandbox (CPU-only, no installed ML stack, network disabled) the experiment cannot be executed. The `track.md` note confirms execution is not required.\\n- **Asm-7** We will treat a win as Δ acc ≥ 0.5 percentage points on any single task and a CS-mean win as Δ_mean ≥ 1.0 pp, since below these thresholds variance / harness version drift dominates.\\n\\nItems I am **uncertain about** (could differ from the paper — please confirm):\\n\\n- **U-1** Whether the paper used exactly this CS subset or added/dropped tasks (needs topic `:setup_2`).\\n- **U-2** Whether the paper fuses 4 vs. 5 vs. other LLMs at 7B; the exact list of base LLMs; whether it's \\\"OpenFuse\\\"-style data or instruction data (needs topic `:setup_9`).\\n- **U-3** Whether the paper reports `acc_norm` for all tasks or uses a specific metric mix.\\n- **U-4** Whether there is a published zero-shot CS mean for FuseLLM-7B and Llama-2-7B that we could pre-register against. If yes and you provide them, I'll add a one-sided tension check (pre-specified equivalence margin of 1.0 pp).\\n- **U-5** Whether HellaSwag's \\\"validation\\\" or \\\"train\\\" split is used as the eval portion per the harness version.\\n- **U-6** Whether WinoGrande is `winogrande_xl` (the default) or a specific size.\\n- **U-7** Whether the paper's commentary distinguishes \\\"Commonsense\\\" from \\\"Extended\\\" benches, and whether BoolQ/StoryCloze/etc. should be added — I currently treat CS as the seven tasks in §2 and do **not** include BoolQ or StoryCloze unless you say so.\\n\\nItems that **cannot be sourced from the provided materials** (need your confirmation):\\n\\n- **S-1.** The exact set of source LLMs fused to produce FuseLLM-7B and the fusion recipe — defer to topic `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`.\\n- **S-2.** The exact CS benchmark list, ordering, and metric choice — defer to topic `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2`.\\n- **S-3.** The published reference numbers for FuseLLM-7B and Llama-2-7B on this suite (if they exist), which would let us pre-register against them.\\n\\n## 8. Deliverables if the experiment were run (for reference)\\n\\n- A per-task accuracy table (7 tasks × 2 models) with `acc_norm` and `acc` columns.\\n- CS-mean (uniform average over the 7 tasks).\\n- A wins/ties/losses count on the seven tasks.\\n- A short prose answer to the research question using the pre-registered criterion in Asm-7.\\n\\nIf the topic chunks `:setup_2` and `:setup_9` become available, I'll tighten §2/§5/A-3/U-1..U-7 and convert assumptions into verified facts before producing the locked final design.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Asks for you before I lock this down into a result-stage design:**\\n\\n1. Confirm the CS suite in §2 — or supply topic `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2`.\\n2. Confirm the fused-models list and fusion recipe at 7B — or supply topic `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`.\\n3. Confirm that \\\"zero-shot\\\" with `num_fewshot=0` and loglikelihood-based MCQ scoring is the intended protocol.\\n4. Confirm whether to add BoolQ / StoryCloze / others, or to keep CS strictly to the seven tasks in §2.\\n5. Confirm the decision criterion in Asm-7 (per-task and CS-mean thresholds), or supply the paper's own framing.\\n\",\"evidence\":\"Repository inspection: only /workspace/task.json exists; documents.track.md metadata explicitly states a design-only task with no source files. Deep filesystem search for *.pdf/*.md/*.txt outside system dirs found nothing. The two researcher_topics (iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2 and :setup_9) reference what is almost certainly the FuseLLM paper (Wan et al., ICLR 2024), but no chunk text for those topics is present in /workspace, /tmp, /home, or elsewhere on the system, and network is disabled. No HuggingFace / model / dataset artifacts exist locally. Therefore every \\\"convention\\\" cited above is from general public knowledge of FuseLLM and lm-evaluation-harness defaults, not from provided materials, and this is flagged in §5 and §7 accordingly. No experiment was executed; no accuracy numbers are reported or fabricated.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Asm-7: A \\\"win\\\" threshold of Δ acc ≥ 0.5 pp per task and Δ CS-mean ≥ 1.0 pp; below that, harness version drift dominates.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"Asm-6: ≥1 A100-40GB-equivalent is available per model; in the actual sandbox this is moot because no execution is required.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Asm-5: The lm-evaluation-harness tasks named are present and stable in the harness version we will pin.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Asm-4: FuseLLM-7B exists as an accessible checkpoint. If it does not, scope grows beyond a fair comparison.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Asm-3: Loglikelihood ranking over full-continuation strings (acc / acc_norm) is the correct scoring rule for MCQ CS tasks; not free-form generation.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Asm-2: \\\"Zero-shot\\\" means num_fewshot=0 in lm-evaluation-harness.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Asm-1: The CS suite (HellaSwag, ARC-C, ARC-E, OBQA, PIQA, SIQA, WinoGrande) is the intended evaluation surface, even though the topic chunk was not provided.</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"S-3 (no source available): Published reference numbers for both models on this suite.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"S-2 (no source available): Exact CS benchmark list — topic :setup_2 needed.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"S-1 (no source available): Source LLMs and fusion recipe — topic :setup_9 needed.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U-7: Whether the paper's notion of \\\"Commonsense\\\" includes BoolQ, StoryCloze, or extends to an \\\"Extended\\\" bench.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U-6: WinoGrande size (xl vs other) and partial-scoring toggle.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U-5: HellaSwag split choice and exact lm-eval-harness task IDs.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U-4: Whether published zero-shot CS numbers exist for FuseLLM-7B and Llama-2-7B that we could pre-register against.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U-3: Whether the paper reports acc_norm or a custom mix of metrics.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U-2: Exact list of base LLMs fused at 7B and the fusion corpus/recipe (defer to topic :setup_9).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U-1: Exact CS subset used by the FuseLLM paper and the ordering (defer to topic :setup_2).</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-d065b5e2-d8b5-4dd3-877a-d0df42ed7983", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
