{"id": "18a8bcb8-7788-428d-bfca-9c0f5cf3816c", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:43:11.751750", "source": "user", "parent_id": "a11e7afa-c2ef-4ce8-98a4-03447ec4295a", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved with these decisions on your 5 asks so we don't loop another round of clarification. Then produce the final locked design as the deliverable (no execution). Decisions on your asks: (1) CS suite accepted as the 7-task suite in §2 (HellaSwag, ARC-C, ARC-E, OBQA, PIQA, SIQA, WinoGrande); keep BoolQ/StoryCloze explicitly out of the primary comparator and mention only as an optional supplement. (2) Use the standard 7B FuseLLM composition set {Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B} with light SFT + next-token distribution matching in representation space + weight-space averaging; flag it as derived from public convention on the FuseLLM paper since no chunk text was provided, and add a one-line 'topic pending verification: iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9' note. (3) Zero-shot = num_fewshot=0 with lm-evaluation-harness loglikelihood ranking over full-continuation strings and BOS prepending; acc_norm headline where the task exposes it, acc otherwise. (4) Don't expand the primary suite; allow a clearly-labeled 'Extended CS' sensitivity row that only lists BoolQ/StoryCloze and is not the primary endpoint. (5) Decision rule: keep your 0.5 pp per-task / 1.0 pp CS-mean thresholds but also report a purely descriptive wins/ties/losses count and an unweighted CS-mean without a hard-coded significance claim, since deterministic loglikelihood eval does not license a frequentist test across the 7 tasks. Lock the final design with: (a) operationalized question, (b) the pinned benchmark suite with task names, fewshot, metrics, max length, (c) the two models with checkpoint assumptions and pinning, (d) the evaluation protocol including harness, scoring, BOS policy, filters, batching, decoding N/A,