{"id": "97811500-ddfd-4cf6-980d-9e59e4663e24", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:44:19.524301", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "18a8bcb8-7788-428d-bfca-9c0f5cf3816c", "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "\n# Final Locked Design — FuseLLM-7B vs. Llama-2-7B on Commonsense Reasoning (Zero-Shot)\n\n> **Design-only deliverable. No experiment is executed in this design-only task.** This document is the single deliverable for the task. All \"source-supported\" claims are explicitly tagged: where I lean on **public convention of the FuseLLM paper** (Wan et al., ICLR 2024) and **lm-evaluation-harness defaults**, without access to the topic chunks indicated by the researcher (`:setup_2`, `:setup_9`), the line is marked *topic pending verification*.\n\n---\n\n## (a) Operationalized Research Question\n\n> **In a zero-shot commonsense reasoning (CS) evaluation, does FuseLLM-7B outperform Llama-2-7B on the pinned 7-task CS suite?**\n\n- **Population**: 7-task CS suite defined in (b).\n- **Unit of analysis**: per-task accuracy; aggregated CS-mean (uniform mean across the 7 task accuracies).\n- **Estimator**: `Δ_task = acc_FuseLLM‑7B(task) − acc_Llama‑2‑7B(task)`. Primary effect size = unweighted CS-mean of those 7 Δs, denoted `Δ_CS`.\n- **Decision rule** (per researcher decision #5): a *task-level* advantage is reported when `Δ_task ≥ +0.5 pp`; a *suite-level* advantage when `Δ_CS ≥ +1.0 pp`. We **also** report a purely descriptive wins/ties/losses tally and the unweighted CS-mean. We **do not** license a frequentist hypothesis test across only 7 tasks under deterministic loglikelihood scoring with one fixed seed.\n- **Why this operationalization**: zero-shot, loglikelihood-based, same-scale comparison isolates model identity as the only free variable.\n\n---\n\n## (b) Pinned Benchmark Suite\n\nPrimary endpoint — **Commonsense Reasoning (CS)**, 7 tasks, all `num_fewshot=0`.\n\n| # | Task | Harness task key | num_fewshot | Metric (headline) | #choices | Notes on filter / split |\n|---|------|-------------------|-------------|-------------------|----------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | HellaSwag | `hellaswag` | 0 | `acc_norm` (length-norm) | 4 | Validate split; harness's context-presence filter on. |\n| 2 | ARC-Challenge | `arc_challenge` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 4 | Validate split. |\n| 3 | ARC-Easy | `arc_easy` | 0 | `acc` (no `acc_norm` variant on `arc_easy` head) | 4 | Validate split. `acc_norm` reported as a sensitivity check. |\n| 4 | OpenBookQA | `openbookqa` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 4 | Validate split. |\n| 5 | PIQA | `piqa` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 2 | Validate split. |\n| 6 | SIQA | `social_iqa` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 2 | Validate split. |\n| 7 | WinoGrande (XL) | `winogrande` | 0 | `acc` | 2 | `winogrande_xl` split; partial-scoring **off** by default. |\n\nCS-mean = unweighted arithmetic mean of `acc` or `acc_norm` (per the table above) across the 7 tasks.\n\n**Maximum sequence length**: `max_length = 2048` tokens for all tasks (none of these tasks truncate at 2048 in zero-shot). The model context window is unused for truncations at this length.\n\n**Optional sensitivity row — \"Extended CS\" (not a primary endpoint)**: `boolq` and `storycloze` (StoryCloze ROCStories 2016 split). Reported in a separate labeled row of the analysis table, **not** mixed into the 7-task CS-mean.\n\n### Primary suite membership is **locked** per researcher decision #1 (no BoolQ/StoryCloze in the primary comparator).\n\n---\n\n## (c) Models — Baseline and Treatment, with Checkpoint Pinning\n\n### Baseline\n- **Model**: Llama-2-7B.\n- **Identifier**: `meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf` (HF canonical name; the prior-generation `huggyllama/llama-7b` is **not** an acceptable substitute — Llama-2 weights must be used).\n- **Tokenizer**: shipped with the model (`add_bos_token=True`).\n- **Weights pinning**: single floating-point precision at eval: **fp16** (matches the published CS numbers, public convention).\n\n### Treatment\n- **Model**: FuseLLM-7B, fused from the standard 7B composition set.\n- **Public-convention composition set** (researcher decision #2; *topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`*):\n  `{Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B}`.\n- **Public-convention fusion recipe** (*topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`*):\n  1. **Light SFT** of each source LLM on the fusion alignment corpus (commonly referred to as **OpenFuse** in public descriptions; specifics not in this workspace).\n  2. **Next-token distribution matching in representation space** between the lightweight SFT'd sources and a target, optimized at scale.\n  3. **Weight-space averaging** at scale.\n- **Tokenizer**: FuseLLM-7B ships its own tokenizer (typically the one used during fusion). If it is the Llama tokenizer (Llama-2/3), we use it; otherwise we use the shipped one and document the swap.\n- **Weights pinning**: fp16 at eval to match the baseline.\n\n### Pinning policy common to both models\n- **No chat/instruct templates applied**: zero-shot evaluation scores continuations under the base LM prior, so no `<s>[INST]…[/INST]`-style prompt formatting is added. This is consistent with the published zero-shot numbers we pre-register against (public convention).\n- **No additional fine-tuning of either model on task data** (no in-context demonstrations beyond `num_fewshot=0`).\n- **Single checkpoint, single hash**: we record the SHA-256 of `model.safetensors` (or `pytorch_model.bin` if safetensors is unavailable) and the commit/revision hash of the model repo in the report.\n- **Determinism basis**: scored-token logits are deterministic for fp16 inference under a fixed input and fixed weights; no sampling.\n\n---\n\n## (d) Evaluation Protocol\n\n**Evaluator**: **EleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness** (the harness used by FuseLLM-style CS evals and the de-facto reference for these benchmarks).\n\n### Generalized config\n- **Mode**: `zero_shot` (`num_fewshot=0`).\n- **Scoring rule**: **loglikelihood ranking over the full continuation string of each choice**, conditioned on the prompt. The selected answer is argmax over the per-choice mean NLL (length-normalized).\n- **BOS policy**: `add_bos_token=True` (harness default; matches public convention).\n- **Tokenizer-side whitespace strip**: harness default (`strip_whitespace=True` on prefixes).\n- **Filters**: per-task harness defaults only. Specifically:\n  - HellaSwag: `filter_list=[\"if_xy_only_check_feminine_plural_match\"]` (harness default; the harness's HellaSwag setup applies the standard context-presence filter, \"punctuation-and-articles\", only when the config flag enables it — we leave it at defaults).\n  - WinoGrande: partial-credit **off**.\n  - ARC: no row filtering additional to harness default.\n- **Decoding**: **not used** for the primary comparator — loglikelihood scoring is non-generative. Documented as \"decoding N/A\" rather than \"unspecified\" to lock the protocol.\n- **Batching**: per-device batch size 8. Where 2048-token context and `batch_size=8` exceeds memory (it should not at 7B on A100-40GB), fall back to 4 then 2 with no other change.\n- **Determinism / seed**: `seed=42`. Under loglikelihood scoring and fp16, results are bit-stable per environment; we record versions of all libraries.\n- **Pinned versions** (public convention; concrete pins set at experiment-run time, but the policy is locked here):\n  - `torch == 2.1.x` (CUDA 11.8 build)\n  - `transformers == 4.36.x`\n  - `lm-eval == 0.4.x` (≥0.4.0; specific pin captured at run time)\n  - `accelerate == 0.24.x`\n  - `tokenizers == 0.15.x`\n  - `numpy`, `datasets` matching `lm-eval`'s pin set\n  A `requirements.lock` will be committed and the SHA-256 of the lockfile is reported in the final write-up.\n\n### Per-task concrete config (locked)\n- **HellaSwag**: `task=hellaswag, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`. lm-eval-harness's default HSC prompt and the per-choice full-string continuation.\n- **ARC-C**: `task=arc_challenge, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\n- **ARC-E**: `task=arc_easy, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc` (with `acc_norm` as a sensitivity row).\n- **OBQA**: `task=openbookqa, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\n- **PIQA**: `task=piqa, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\n- **SIQA**: `task=social_iqa, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\n- **WinoGrande**: `task=winogrande, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc` on the xl split; partial-scoring off.\n\n---\n\n## (e) Controls and Confound Checklist\n\n| # | Confound | Control |\n|---|----------|---------|\n| 1 | Different prompts across models | Harness YAML templates are identical; baseline and treatment see the *same* rendered prompt for every example. |\n| 2 | Different scoring rules | Both models use loglikelihood ranking over the same sentinels per task (`acc_norm` where it exists, `acc` otherwise). |\n| 3 | Different tokenizers | Each model uses **its own** tokenizer (FuseLLM-7B is not re-tokenized with Llama-2's tokenizer). Documented; consistent with the published methodology. |\n| 4 | Different precision | Both in fp16 at eval. |\n| 5 | Different few-shot leakage | `num_fewshot=0` universally. |\n| 6 | Different filters / row drops | Per-task defaults held constant. |\n| 7 | Different splits | Validation for HellaSwag / ARC / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA, `winogrande_xl` for WinoGrande, as held by the harness defaults. |\n| 8 | Sampling noise | Not applicable — loglikelihood scoring is deterministic under fixed weights. |\n| 9 | Checkpoint drift | Single SHA-256 + repo revision hash per model is recorded. |\n| 10 | Truncation differences | `max_length=2048` is below the input length cap for all 7 tasks. No truncate-and-discard logs expected. |\n| 11 | Library-version drift | `requirements.lock` SHA-256 recorded; reran-on-failure protocol: if the harness's own Llama-2-7B smoke test drifts >0.1 pp from its prior harness-version envelope, switch to the harness-version-pinned env and rerun both models. |\n| 12 | Chat template bleeding | None applied; `apply_chat_template=False` enforced. |\n| 13 | Random seed of harness's orderings | `seed=42`; harness order is deterministic from the dataset fixture. |\n| 14 | Operator degree of freedom | All knobs are pinned *before* seeing the numbers; any deviation after the fact triggers a re-run. |\n\n---\n\n## (f) Analysis Plan\n\n### Outcome variables\n- **Per-task**: `acc` and `acc_norm` (both computed by the harness; acc_norm is headline where it exists).\n- **CS-mean**: unweighted mean over the 7 headline task scores.\n\n### Primary comparison\n- `Δ_task = FuseLLM-7B_headline − Llama-2-7B_headline` per task.\n- `Δ_CS = mean(Δ_task, over 7 tasks)`.\n\n### Decision rule (locked per researcher decision #5)\n- A **task-level** advantage is reported if `Δ_task ≥ +0.5 pp`.\n- A **suite-level** advantage is reported if `Δ_CS ≥ +1.0 pp`.\n- **Descriptive-only**: count of wins / ties / losses across the 7 tasks, where \"win\" = `Δ_task ≥ +0.5 pp`, \"tie\" = `|Δ_task| < 0.5 pp`, \"loss\" = `Δ_task ≤ −0.5 pp`. No p-value; **no frequentist claim** licensed by this design.\n\n### Sensitivity checks (not primary)\n1. `acc` vs `acc_norm` recompute for tasks that expose `acc_norm` (HellaSwag / ARC-C / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA). Tabulate to show headline robustness; does not change `Δ_CS` computation unless the headline metric is itself switched.\n2. **Extended CS row** (researcher decision #4): BoolQ and StoryCloze are listed in a labeled row of the reporting table and **not** mixed into `Δ_CS`.\n3. **Direction-of-difference consistency**: tally of `sign(Δ_task)` across the 7 tasks to flag whether the result is mostly directional rather than based on a single big-task swing.\n4. **Smoke envelope** for Llama-2-7B vs the harness-version envelope: a 0.1-pp-level regression indicator, not a primary endpoint.\n\n### Reporting tables\n\n**Table R1 (primary).** 7 rows × 4 columns.\n- Columns: Task | Llama-2-7B (headline acc) | FuseLLM-7B (headline acc) | Δ_task.\n- One row per task.\n\n**Table R2 (analysis).**\n- CS-mean for Llama-2-7B, CS-mean for FuseLLM-7B, `Δ_CS`.\n- Wins / ties / losses count.\n\n**Table R3 (sensitivity).**\n- Per-task acc vs acc_norm restated (for the 5 tasks where acc_norm is exposed).\n- Extended CS row: BoolQ and StoryCloze scores for both models Δs reported in a separately labeled row; these are **not** added to `Δ_CS`.\n\n**Table R4 (provenance).**\n- Model name | Repo ID | Revision / SHA-256 | Tokenizer | Eval precision | Harness version | Lockfile SHA-256.\n\nNo numerical results are reported in this design document — by definition of a design-only task and by the \"do not invent or quote numbers from a source\" instruction.\n\n---\n\n## (g) Compute and Storage Feasibility (executed-out-of-sandbox estimate)\n\nPer researcher note that the sandbox is CPU-only with `network=disabled`, `gpu_enabled=false`, and no preinstalled ML stack — **no execution happens here**. The below is the feasibility for the **planned** run on the intended hardware (single A100-40GB per model, weights only).\n\n### Storage\n\n| Artifact | Size | Notes |\n|----------|------|-------|\n| Llama-2-7B checkpoint (fp16) | ~13 GB | safetensors shard set |\n| FuseLLM-7B checkpoint (fp16) | ~13–14 GB | safetensors shard set, fused-model scale |\n| lm-evaluation-harness datasets cache | ~1–2 GB | cached once, shared by both model evals |\n| Outputs (per-model CS results JSON + CSV) | <100 MB | trivial |\n\nTotal disk footprint on the eval host: **~30 GB**, comfortably within a single A100-40GB host's local NVMe (typically >500 GB free).\n\n### Compute (wall-clock, per model, on 1× A100-40GB, fp16)\n\nApproximate question counts driving compute (loglikelihood ranking over full continuations):\n\n| Task | #questions | #choices | Forward passes ~ |\n|------|-----------|----------|------------------|\n| HellaSwag | ~10,042 | 4 | ~40,200 |\n| ARC-C | 1,172 | 4 | ~4,700 |\n| ARC-E | 2,376 | 4 | ~9,500 |\n| OBQA | 500 | 4 | ~2,000 |\n| PIQA | 1,838 | 2 | ~3,700 |\n| SIQA | 1,954 | 2 | ~3,900 |\n| WinoGrande | 1,267 | 2 | ~2,500 |\n| **Total** | | | **~66,500 / model** |\n\nOperational profile (public convention for fp16 7B inference on A100-40GB):\n- 7B fp16 forward pass at length 256, `batch_size=8`: order-of-magnitude wall time ~5–10 ms per `bs × seq` batch using vLLM-style optimized kernels; ~20–40 ms per item with a stock `transformers` `\"eager\"` or `\"sdpa\"` path.\n- Total forward passes: ~66,500. End-to-end CS suite per model on 1× A100-40GB (no retraining): **~0.5–2 hours per model** depending on the exact kernel path.\n- Two models ⇒ **~1–4 hours total wall time** on a single A100-40GB host sequentially, **or ~1–2 hours** if the two models are run on separate A100-40GB cards in parallel.\n\n### Memory\n\n- 7B fp16 weights: ~13–14 GB.\n- KV cache at `bs=8`, `seq_len=2048`: ~2–4 GB additional.\n- Headroom for activations: comfortably within A100-40GB.\n\n### Sandbox / environment note\n\nThe provided runtime is **bubblewrap, CPU-only, network disabled, with system Python and an empty `/workspace`**. By the design-only nature of this task (`documents.track.md: \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"`), **no execution of this protocol is performed or required in this deliverable.** All numbers and feasibility items above are planning estimates against literature/perf conventions, not measurements.\n\n---\n\n## (h) Consolidated Assumptions, Uncertainties, and Pending-Verification Items\n\n### Locked assumptions (taken as design inputs)\n\n- **A-1** The 7-task CS suite in (b) is the primary endpoint set, as approved per researcher decision #1.\n- **A-2** BoolQ and StoryCloze are reported only as a labeled Extended CS sensitivity row, **not** the primary endpoint, as approved per researcher decision #4.\n- **A-3** \"Zero-shot\" means `num_fewshot=0` in lm-evaluation-harness.\n- **A-4** Scoring rule for multi-choice CS tasks is loglikelihood ranking over full-continuation strings, with `acc_norm` headline where the task exposes it, `acc` otherwise. Decoding is **N/A** for the primary comparator.\n- **A-5** Each model uses **its own** tokenizer at eval; `add_bos_token=True`; `apply_chat_template=False`.\n- **A-6** fp16 for both models at eval.\n- **A-7** Pinned environment policy (`requirements.lock` + SHA-256) is part of the design; reseed only on harness-version drift >0.1 pp.\n- **A-8** Decision thresholds `Δ_task = +0.5 pp`, `Δ_CS = +1.0 pp`, with descriptive wins/ties/losses and **no frequentist test** across only 7 deterministic tasks.\n- **A-9** Public-convention fusion recipe at 7B: light SFT of each source LLM on the OpenFuse-style alignment corpus (public convention; **topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`**), next-token distribution matching in representation space, then weight-space averaging at scale.\n\n### Open uncertainties / pending verification\n\n- **S-1** *(topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`)* — exact identity of source LLMs in FuseLLM-7B and the detailed fusion recipe; we are using the standard 7B composition {Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B} with light SFT + next-token distribution matching + weight-space averaging, **derived from public convention of the FuseLLM paper**, not from the provided topic chunk (which was not available in the workspace).\n- **S-2** *(topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2`)* — exact CS benchmark list and ordering used by the FuseLLM authors; we are using HellaSwag / ARC-C / ARC-E / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA / WinoGrande per the published lm-evaluation-harness defaults, **derived from public convention**, not from the provided topic chunk.\n- **S-3** *(no source provided)* — published zero-shot CS reference numbers for Llama-2-7B and FuseLLM-7B on this suite, which could be pre-registered as external anchors. None are quoted in this design.\n\n### Other uncertainties not source-tied but non-blocking\n\n- **U-1** Whether the harness task IDs above correspond exactly to the FuseLLM paper's reported splits (validation vs others for HellaSwag / ARC / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA; WinoGrande `xl` size choice).\n- **U-2** Per-task `acc` vs `acc_norm` choice may differ from the paper's headline mix; we have applied **headline rule**: `acc_norm` if exposed, else `acc`.\n- **U-3** BoolQ / StoryCloze exact scoring convention (`acc`/`acc_norm`/likelihood choice). These are sensitivity only, so this does not affect `Δ_CS`.\n- **U-4** Once the source topic chunks become available, A-1 through A-9 should be re-evaluated against text; deviations will trigger a design revision.\n\n### What this design explicitly refuses to do (compliance)\n\n- No execution; no accuracy numbers claimed, reported, or invented as if from a source.\n- No claim that the FuseLLM paper used exactly this suite without seeing the source (A-1 / S-2 pending verification).\n- No claim of statistical significance across 7 deterministic tasks.\n- No selection of Llama-1 in place of Llama-2; Llama-2-7B is required.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe design is locked. It scores FuseLLM-7B and Llama-2-7B on the 7-task zero-shot CS suite with lm-evaluation-harness, loglikelihood ranking, BOS-prepended, `acc_norm`/`acc` headline per task, identical prompts / scoring / precision / harness version / seed for both models, no chat templates, no few-shot examples. Outcomes are per-task `Δ`, the unweighted CS-mean `Δ_CS`, wins/ties/losses, decision thresholds of 0.5 pp / 1.0 pp, plus an Extended CS sensitivity row containing BoolQ and StoryCloze. Compute fits one A100-40GB per model with weights only and no retraining; the actual sandbox is CPU-only with no execution expected. Three source items (S-1, S-2, S-3) remain tagged *topic pending verification* and are the explicit, named gaps between the locked design and any hypothetically fully source-grounded version of it.\n", "evidence": "Repository inspection confirmed only /workspace/task.json is present; documents.track.md metadata states 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required'; no source PDF, no extracted topic chunks for iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2 or :setup_9 exist in the workspace, /tmp, /home, or anywhere accessible; network is disabled. Therefore every paper-derived detail in this design is taken from public conventions of the FuseLLM paper (Wan et al., ICLR 2024) and lm-evaluation-harness defaults, and is explicitly tagged 'topic pending verification' where the corresponding source chunk would have resolved an uncertainty. No experiment was executed; no accuracy numbers are stated or fabricated. The 5 researcher decisions on Ask #1..#5 are reflected directly: (1) 7-task primary CS suite, (2) {Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B} with SFT + NextDistMatch + weighted averaging, (3) zero-shot=num_fewshot=0 / ll-ranking / BOS / acc_norm-where-exposed, (4) BoolQ+StoryCloze kept as a labeled sensitivity row only, (5) 0.5 pp / 1.0 pp thresholds + descriptive wins/ties/losses + no frequentist claim across deterministic 7-task eval. All 8 deliverable sections (a-h) per the researcher's lock-in spec are present.", "assumptions": ["A-1: The 7-task CS suite (HellaSwag, ARC-C, ARC-E, OBQA, PIQA, SIQA, WinoGrande) is the primary endpoint set, per researcher decision #1.", "A-2: BoolQ and StoryCloze appear only as a labeled Extended CS sensitivity row, not as primary endpoints, per researcher decision #4.", "A-3: 'Zero-shot' means num_fewshot=0 in lm-evaluation-harness.", "A-4: Scoring rule for multi-choice CS tasks is loglikelihood ranking over full-continuation strings; decoding is N/A for the primary comparator.", "A-5: Each model uses its own tokenizer at eval; add_bos_token=True; apply_chat_template=False.", "A-6: Both models evaluated in fp16.", "A-7: Pinned environment policy via requirements.lock; reseed-on-drift only beyond 0.1 pp.", "A-8: Decision thresholds Δ_task=+0.5 pp and Δ_CS=+1.0 pp; descriptive wins/ties/losses; no frequentist test across 7 deterministic tasks.", "A-9: Public-convention 7B fusion recipe (light SFT + next-token distribution matching + weight-space averaging) is taken as the design input; topic pending verification: iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9."], "uncertainties": ["S-1 — topic pending verification: iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9: exact source LLMs in FuseLLM-7B and detailed fusion recipe; standard 7B composition {Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B} derived from public convention.", "S-2 — topic pending verification: iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2: exact CS benchmark list and ordering used by the FuseLLM authors; 7-task suite derived from public convention.", "S-3 — no source provided: published zero-shot CS reference numbers for either model; none quoted.", "U-1: Harness task IDs vs. paper-reported splits (e.g., HellaSwag validation vs other; WinoGrande xl size).", "U-2: Per-task acc vs acc_norm choice vs the paper's headline mix.", "U-3: BoolQ / StoryCloze scoring convention; these are sensitivity-only and do not enter Δ_CS.", "U-4: Once source chunks become available, A-1..A-9 should be re-evaluated; deviations trigger a revision."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-8f71ed2c-b798-472f-b603-ecb0524f0e61", "tool_call": {"id": "call-8f71ed2c-b798-472f-b603-ecb0524f0e61", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Deliver locked final experiment design\", \"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"\\n# Final Locked Design \\u2014 FuseLLM-7B vs. Llama-2-7B on Commonsense Reasoning (Zero-Shot)\\n\\n> **Design-only deliverable. No experiment is executed in this design-only task.** This document is the single deliverable for the task. All \\\"source-supported\\\" claims are explicitly tagged: where I lean on **public convention of the FuseLLM paper** (Wan et al., ICLR 2024) and **lm-evaluation-harness defaults**, without access to the topic chunks indicated by the researcher (`:setup_2`, `:setup_9`), the line is marked *topic pending verification*.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (a) Operationalized Research Question\\n\\n> **In a zero-shot commonsense reasoning (CS) evaluation, does FuseLLM-7B outperform Llama-2-7B on the pinned 7-task CS suite?**\\n\\n- **Population**: 7-task CS suite defined in (b).\\n- **Unit of analysis**: per-task accuracy; aggregated CS-mean (uniform mean across the 7 task accuracies).\\n- **Estimator**: `\\u0394_task = acc_FuseLLM\\u20117B(task) \\u2212 acc_Llama\\u20112\\u20117B(task)`. Primary effect size = unweighted CS-mean of those 7 \\u0394s, denoted `\\u0394_CS`.\\n- **Decision rule** (per researcher decision #5): a *task-level* advantage is reported when `\\u0394_task \\u2265 +0.5 pp`; a *suite-level* advantage when `\\u0394_CS \\u2265 +1.0 pp`. We **also** report a purely descriptive wins/ties/losses tally and the unweighted CS-mean. We **do not** license a frequentist hypothesis test across only 7 tasks under deterministic loglikelihood scoring with one fixed seed.\\n- **Why this operationalization**: zero-shot, loglikelihood-based, same-scale comparison isolates model identity as the only free variable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (b) Pinned Benchmark Suite\\n\\nPrimary endpoint \\u2014 **Commonsense Reasoning (CS)**, 7 tasks, all `num_fewshot=0`.\\n\\n| # | Task | Harness task key | num_fewshot | Metric (headline) | #choices | Notes on filter / split |\\n|---|------|-------------------|-------------|-------------------|----------|--------------------------|\\n| 1 | HellaSwag | `hellaswag` | 0 | `acc_norm` (length-norm) | 4 | Validate split; harness's context-presence filter on. |\\n| 2 | ARC-Challenge | `arc_challenge` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 4 | Validate split. |\\n| 3 | ARC-Easy | `arc_easy` | 0 | `acc` (no `acc_norm` variant on `arc_easy` head) | 4 | Validate split. `acc_norm` reported as a sensitivity check. |\\n| 4 | OpenBookQA | `openbookqa` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 4 | Validate split. |\\n| 5 | PIQA | `piqa` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 2 | Validate split. |\\n| 6 | SIQA | `social_iqa` | 0 | `acc_norm` | 2 | Validate split. |\\n| 7 | WinoGrande (XL) | `winogrande` | 0 | `acc` | 2 | `winogrande_xl` split; partial-scoring **off** by default. |\\n\\nCS-mean = unweighted arithmetic mean of `acc` or `acc_norm` (per the table above) across the 7 tasks.\\n\\n**Maximum sequence length**: `max_length = 2048` tokens for all tasks (none of these tasks truncate at 2048 in zero-shot). The model context window is unused for truncations at this length.\\n\\n**Optional sensitivity row \\u2014 \\\"Extended CS\\\" (not a primary endpoint)**: `boolq` and `storycloze` (StoryCloze ROCStories 2016 split). Reported in a separate labeled row of the analysis table, **not** mixed into the 7-task CS-mean.\\n\\n### Primary suite membership is **locked** per researcher decision #1 (no BoolQ/StoryCloze in the primary comparator).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (c) Models \\u2014 Baseline and Treatment, with Checkpoint Pinning\\n\\n### Baseline\\n- **Model**: Llama-2-7B.\\n- **Identifier**: `meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf` (HF canonical name; the prior-generation `huggyllama/llama-7b` is **not** an acceptable substitute \\u2014 Llama-2 weights must be used).\\n- **Tokenizer**: shipped with the model (`add_bos_token=True`).\\n- **Weights pinning**: single floating-point precision at eval: **fp16** (matches the published CS numbers, public convention).\\n\\n### Treatment\\n- **Model**: FuseLLM-7B, fused from the standard 7B composition set.\\n- **Public-convention composition set** (researcher decision #2; *topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`*):\\n  `{Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B}`.\\n- **Public-convention fusion recipe** (*topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`*):\\n  1. **Light SFT** of each source LLM on the fusion alignment corpus (commonly referred to as **OpenFuse** in public descriptions; specifics not in this workspace).\\n  2. **Next-token distribution matching in representation space** between the lightweight SFT'd sources and a target, optimized at scale.\\n  3. **Weight-space averaging** at scale.\\n- **Tokenizer**: FuseLLM-7B ships its own tokenizer (typically the one used during fusion). If it is the Llama tokenizer (Llama-2/3), we use it; otherwise we use the shipped one and document the swap.\\n- **Weights pinning**: fp16 at eval to match the baseline.\\n\\n### Pinning policy common to both models\\n- **No chat/instruct templates applied**: zero-shot evaluation scores continuations under the base LM prior, so no `<s>[INST]\\u2026[/INST]`-style prompt formatting is added. This is consistent with the published zero-shot numbers we pre-register against (public convention).\\n- **No additional fine-tuning of either model on task data** (no in-context demonstrations beyond `num_fewshot=0`).\\n- **Single checkpoint, single hash**: we record the SHA-256 of `model.safetensors` (or `pytorch_model.bin` if safetensors is unavailable) and the commit/revision hash of the model repo in the report.\\n- **Determinism basis**: scored-token logits are deterministic for fp16 inference under a fixed input and fixed weights; no sampling.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (d) Evaluation Protocol\\n\\n**Evaluator**: **EleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness** (the harness used by FuseLLM-style CS evals and the de-facto reference for these benchmarks).\\n\\n### Generalized config\\n- **Mode**: `zero_shot` (`num_fewshot=0`).\\n- **Scoring rule**: **loglikelihood ranking over the full continuation string of each choice**, conditioned on the prompt. The selected answer is argmax over the per-choice mean NLL (length-normalized).\\n- **BOS policy**: `add_bos_token=True` (harness default; matches public convention).\\n- **Tokenizer-side whitespace strip**: harness default (`strip_whitespace=True` on prefixes).\\n- **Filters**: per-task harness defaults only. Specifically:\\n  - HellaSwag: `filter_list=[\\\"if_xy_only_check_feminine_plural_match\\\"]` (harness default; the harness's HellaSwag setup applies the standard context-presence filter, \\\"punctuation-and-articles\\\", only when the config flag enables it \\u2014 we leave it at defaults).\\n  - WinoGrande: partial-credit **off**.\\n  - ARC: no row filtering additional to harness default.\\n- **Decoding**: **not used** for the primary comparator \\u2014 loglikelihood scoring is non-generative. Documented as \\\"decoding N/A\\\" rather than \\\"unspecified\\\" to lock the protocol.\\n- **Batching**: per-device batch size 8. Where 2048-token context and `batch_size=8` exceeds memory (it should not at 7B on A100-40GB), fall back to 4 then 2 with no other change.\\n- **Determinism / seed**: `seed=42`. Under loglikelihood scoring and fp16, results are bit-stable per environment; we record versions of all libraries.\\n- **Pinned versions** (public convention; concrete pins set at experiment-run time, but the policy is locked here):\\n  - `torch == 2.1.x` (CUDA 11.8 build)\\n  - `transformers == 4.36.x`\\n  - `lm-eval == 0.4.x` (\\u22650.4.0; specific pin captured at run time)\\n  - `accelerate == 0.24.x`\\n  - `tokenizers == 0.15.x`\\n  - `numpy`, `datasets` matching `lm-eval`'s pin set\\n  A `requirements.lock` will be committed and the SHA-256 of the lockfile is reported in the final write-up.\\n\\n### Per-task concrete config (locked)\\n- **HellaSwag**: `task=hellaswag, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`. lm-eval-harness's default HSC prompt and the per-choice full-string continuation.\\n- **ARC-C**: `task=arc_challenge, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\\n- **ARC-E**: `task=arc_easy, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc` (with `acc_norm` as a sensitivity row).\\n- **OBQA**: `task=openbookqa, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\\n- **PIQA**: `task=piqa, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\\n- **SIQA**: `task=social_iqa, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc_norm`.\\n- **WinoGrande**: `task=winogrande, num_fewshot=0, metric=acc` on the xl split; partial-scoring off.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (e) Controls and Confound Checklist\\n\\n| # | Confound | Control |\\n|---|----------|---------|\\n| 1 | Different prompts across models | Harness YAML templates are identical; baseline and treatment see the *same* rendered prompt for every example. |\\n| 2 | Different scoring rules | Both models use loglikelihood ranking over the same sentinels per task (`acc_norm` where it exists, `acc` otherwise). |\\n| 3 | Different tokenizers | Each model uses **its own** tokenizer (FuseLLM-7B is not re-tokenized with Llama-2's tokenizer). Documented; consistent with the published methodology. |\\n| 4 | Different precision | Both in fp16 at eval. |\\n| 5 | Different few-shot leakage | `num_fewshot=0` universally. |\\n| 6 | Different filters / row drops | Per-task defaults held constant. |\\n| 7 | Different splits | Validation for HellaSwag / ARC / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA, `winogrande_xl` for WinoGrande, as held by the harness defaults. |\\n| 8 | Sampling noise | Not applicable \\u2014 loglikelihood scoring is deterministic under fixed weights. |\\n| 9 | Checkpoint drift | Single SHA-256 + repo revision hash per model is recorded. |\\n| 10 | Truncation differences | `max_length=2048` is below the input length cap for all 7 tasks. No truncate-and-discard logs expected. |\\n| 11 | Library-version drift | `requirements.lock` SHA-256 recorded; reran-on-failure protocol: if the harness's own Llama-2-7B smoke test drifts >0.1 pp from its prior harness-version envelope, switch to the harness-version-pinned env and rerun both models. |\\n| 12 | Chat template bleeding | None applied; `apply_chat_template=False` enforced. |\\n| 13 | Random seed of harness's orderings | `seed=42`; harness order is deterministic from the dataset fixture. |\\n| 14 | Operator degree of freedom | All knobs are pinned *before* seeing the numbers; any deviation after the fact triggers a re-run. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (f) Analysis Plan\\n\\n### Outcome variables\\n- **Per-task**: `acc` and `acc_norm` (both computed by the harness; acc_norm is headline where it exists).\\n- **CS-mean**: unweighted mean over the 7 headline task scores.\\n\\n### Primary comparison\\n- `\\u0394_task = FuseLLM-7B_headline \\u2212 Llama-2-7B_headline` per task.\\n- `\\u0394_CS = mean(\\u0394_task, over 7 tasks)`.\\n\\n### Decision rule (locked per researcher decision #5)\\n- A **task-level** advantage is reported if `\\u0394_task \\u2265 +0.5 pp`.\\n- A **suite-level** advantage is reported if `\\u0394_CS \\u2265 +1.0 pp`.\\n- **Descriptive-only**: count of wins / ties / losses across the 7 tasks, where \\\"win\\\" = `\\u0394_task \\u2265 +0.5 pp`, \\\"tie\\\" = `|\\u0394_task| < 0.5 pp`, \\\"loss\\\" = `\\u0394_task \\u2264 \\u22120.5 pp`. No p-value; **no frequentist claim** licensed by this design.\\n\\n### Sensitivity checks (not primary)\\n1. `acc` vs `acc_norm` recompute for tasks that expose `acc_norm` (HellaSwag / ARC-C / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA). Tabulate to show headline robustness; does not change `\\u0394_CS` computation unless the headline metric is itself switched.\\n2. **Extended CS row** (researcher decision #4): BoolQ and StoryCloze are listed in a labeled row of the reporting table and **not** mixed into `\\u0394_CS`.\\n3. **Direction-of-difference consistency**: tally of `sign(\\u0394_task)` across the 7 tasks to flag whether the result is mostly directional rather than based on a single big-task swing.\\n4. **Smoke envelope** for Llama-2-7B vs the harness-version envelope: a 0.1-pp-level regression indicator, not a primary endpoint.\\n\\n### Reporting tables\\n\\n**Table R1 (primary).** 7 rows \\u00d7 4 columns.\\n- Columns: Task | Llama-2-7B (headline acc) | FuseLLM-7B (headline acc) | \\u0394_task.\\n- One row per task.\\n\\n**Table R2 (analysis).**\\n- CS-mean for Llama-2-7B, CS-mean for FuseLLM-7B, `\\u0394_CS`.\\n- Wins / ties / losses count.\\n\\n**Table R3 (sensitivity).**\\n- Per-task acc vs acc_norm restated (for the 5 tasks where acc_norm is exposed).\\n- Extended CS row: BoolQ and StoryCloze scores for both models \\u0394s reported in a separately labeled row; these are **not** added to `\\u0394_CS`.\\n\\n**Table R4 (provenance).**\\n- Model name | Repo ID | Revision / SHA-256 | Tokenizer | Eval precision | Harness version | Lockfile SHA-256.\\n\\nNo numerical results are reported in this design document \\u2014 by definition of a design-only task and by the \\\"do not invent or quote numbers from a source\\\" instruction.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (g) Compute and Storage Feasibility (executed-out-of-sandbox estimate)\\n\\nPer researcher note that the sandbox is CPU-only with `network=disabled`, `gpu_enabled=false`, and no preinstalled ML stack \\u2014 **no execution happens here**. The below is the feasibility for the **planned** run on the intended hardware (single A100-40GB per model, weights only).\\n\\n### Storage\\n\\n| Artifact | Size | Notes |\\n|----------|------|-------|\\n| Llama-2-7B checkpoint (fp16) | ~13 GB | safetensors shard set |\\n| FuseLLM-7B checkpoint (fp16) | ~13\\u201314 GB | safetensors shard set, fused-model scale |\\n| lm-evaluation-harness datasets cache | ~1\\u20132 GB | cached once, shared by both model evals |\\n| Outputs (per-model CS results JSON + CSV) | <100 MB | trivial |\\n\\nTotal disk footprint on the eval host: **~30 GB**, comfortably within a single A100-40GB host's local NVMe (typically >500 GB free).\\n\\n### Compute (wall-clock, per model, on 1\\u00d7 A100-40GB, fp16)\\n\\nApproximate question counts driving compute (loglikelihood ranking over full continuations):\\n\\n| Task | #questions | #choices | Forward passes ~ |\\n|------|-----------|----------|------------------|\\n| HellaSwag | ~10,042 | 4 | ~40,200 |\\n| ARC-C | 1,172 | 4 | ~4,700 |\\n| ARC-E | 2,376 | 4 | ~9,500 |\\n| OBQA | 500 | 4 | ~2,000 |\\n| PIQA | 1,838 | 2 | ~3,700 |\\n| SIQA | 1,954 | 2 | ~3,900 |\\n| WinoGrande | 1,267 | 2 | ~2,500 |\\n| **Total** | | | **~66,500 / model** |\\n\\nOperational profile (public convention for fp16 7B inference on A100-40GB):\\n- 7B fp16 forward pass at length 256, `batch_size=8`: order-of-magnitude wall time ~5\\u201310 ms per `bs \\u00d7 seq` batch using vLLM-style optimized kernels; ~20\\u201340 ms per item with a stock `transformers` `\\\"eager\\\"` or `\\\"sdpa\\\"` path.\\n- Total forward passes: ~66,500. End-to-end CS suite per model on 1\\u00d7 A100-40GB (no retraining): **~0.5\\u20132 hours per model** depending on the exact kernel path.\\n- Two models \\u21d2 **~1\\u20134 hours total wall time** on a single A100-40GB host sequentially, **or ~1\\u20132 hours** if the two models are run on separate A100-40GB cards in parallel.\\n\\n### Memory\\n\\n- 7B fp16 weights: ~13\\u201314 GB.\\n- KV cache at `bs=8`, `seq_len=2048`: ~2\\u20134 GB additional.\\n- Headroom for activations: comfortably within A100-40GB.\\n\\n### Sandbox / environment note\\n\\nThe provided runtime is **bubblewrap, CPU-only, network disabled, with system Python and an empty `/workspace`**. By the design-only nature of this task (`documents.track.md: \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\"`), **no execution of this protocol is performed or required in this deliverable.** All numbers and feasibility items above are planning estimates against literature/perf conventions, not measurements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (h) Consolidated Assumptions, Uncertainties, and Pending-Verification Items\\n\\n### Locked assumptions (taken as design inputs)\\n\\n- **A-1** The 7-task CS suite in (b) is the primary endpoint set, as approved per researcher decision #1.\\n- **A-2** BoolQ and StoryCloze are reported only as a labeled Extended CS sensitivity row, **not** the primary endpoint, as approved per researcher decision #4.\\n- **A-3** \\\"Zero-shot\\\" means `num_fewshot=0` in lm-evaluation-harness.\\n- **A-4** Scoring rule for multi-choice CS tasks is loglikelihood ranking over full-continuation strings, with `acc_norm` headline where the task exposes it, `acc` otherwise. Decoding is **N/A** for the primary comparator.\\n- **A-5** Each model uses **its own** tokenizer at eval; `add_bos_token=True`; `apply_chat_template=False`.\\n- **A-6** fp16 for both models at eval.\\n- **A-7** Pinned environment policy (`requirements.lock` + SHA-256) is part of the design; reseed only on harness-version drift >0.1 pp.\\n- **A-8** Decision thresholds `\\u0394_task = +0.5 pp`, `\\u0394_CS = +1.0 pp`, with descriptive wins/ties/losses and **no frequentist test** across only 7 deterministic tasks.\\n- **A-9** Public-convention fusion recipe at 7B: light SFT of each source LLM on the OpenFuse-style alignment corpus (public convention; **topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`**), next-token distribution matching in representation space, then weight-space averaging at scale.\\n\\n### Open uncertainties / pending verification\\n\\n- **S-1** *(topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9`)* \\u2014 exact identity of source LLMs in FuseLLM-7B and the detailed fusion recipe; we are using the standard 7B composition {Llama-2-7B, OpenLLaMA-7B, MPT-7B, Falcon-7B} with light SFT + next-token distribution matching + weight-space averaging, **derived from public convention of the FuseLLM paper**, not from the provided topic chunk (which was not available in the workspace).\\n- **S-2** *(topic pending verification: `iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2`)* \\u2014 exact CS benchmark list and ordering used by the FuseLLM authors; we are using HellaSwag / ARC-C / ARC-E / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA / WinoGrande per the published lm-evaluation-harness defaults, **derived from public convention**, not from the provided topic chunk.\\n- **S-3** *(no source provided)* \\u2014 published zero-shot CS reference numbers for Llama-2-7B and FuseLLM-7B on this suite, which could be pre-registered as external anchors. None are quoted in this design.\\n\\n### Other uncertainties not source-tied but non-blocking\\n\\n- **U-1** Whether the harness task IDs above correspond exactly to the FuseLLM paper's reported splits (validation vs others for HellaSwag / ARC / OBQA / PIQA / SIQA; WinoGrande `xl` size choice).\\n- **U-2** Per-task `acc` vs `acc_norm` choice may differ from the paper's headline mix; we have applied **headline rule**: `acc_norm` if exposed, else `acc`.\\n- **U-3** BoolQ / StoryCloze exact scoring convention (`acc`/`acc_norm`/likelihood choice). These are sensitivity only, so this does not affect `\\u0394_CS`.\\n- **U-4** Once the source topic chunks become available, A-1 through A-9 should be re-evaluated against text; deviations will trigger a design revision.\\n\\n### What this design explicitly refuses to do (compliance)\\n\\n- No execution; no accuracy numbers claimed, reported, or invented as if from a source.\\n- No claim that the FuseLLM paper used exactly this suite without seeing the source (A-1 / S-2 pending verification).\\n- No claim of statistical significance across 7 deterministic tasks.\\n- No selection of Llama-1 in place of Llama-2; Llama-2-7B is required.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe design is locked. It scores FuseLLM-7B and Llama-2-7B on the 7-task zero-shot CS suite with lm-evaluation-harness, loglikelihood ranking, BOS-prepended, `acc_norm`/`acc` headline per task, identical prompts / scoring / precision / harness version / seed for both models, no chat templates, no few-shot examples. Outcomes are per-task `\\u0394`, the unweighted CS-mean `\\u0394_CS`, wins/ties/losses, decision thresholds of 0.5 pp / 1.0 pp, plus an Extended CS sensitivity row containing BoolQ and StoryCloze. Compute fits one A100-40GB per model with weights only and no retraining; the actual sandbox is CPU-only with no execution expected. Three source items (S-1, S-2, S-3) remain tagged *topic pending verification* and are the explicit, named gaps between the locked design and any hypothetically fully source-grounded version of it.\\n\", \"evidence\": \"Repository inspection confirmed only /workspace/task.json is present; documents.track.md metadata states 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required'; no source PDF, no extracted topic chunks for iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2 or :setup_9 exist in the worksp